+-{"id": "AUG-027", "title": "[P1] bundle impact pass is INVISIBLE from the verb: an 'unchanged' verdict at confidence 0.24 is honored with no floor, and cmd_answer prints nothing of the walk (not walked/affects/breaks/skipped), so a real user cannot tell the pass ran", "status": "in_progress", "priority": "P1", "type": null, "created_at": "2026-09-23T04:45:00+00:00", "created_by": null, "description": null, "acceptance_criteria": "Dogfood 2026-09-23 (namespace mccli, bundle B-01 with sibling mcview): `answer --scope bundle` (D-003..D-006) returned in ~1s with zero output beyond 'recorded' while the walk DID execute (function-level probe proved walked=[mcview]) \u2014 JEV scored mccli's sha256->blake3 envelope swap as 'unchanged' against mcview's validate-hash contract at confidence 0.24 and the engine accepted it: no edge, no warning, no line. The same walk invoked at function level (probe_impact.py) wrote AFFECTS edge E-000001 at score 0.50. Two defects stack: (1) bundle_impact_verdict has NO confidence floor \u2014 any verdict >= T_IMPACT_CHANGE threshold logic applies, but a LOW-confidence 'unchanged' is silently final, violating the module's own fail-closed doctrine (an uncertain verdict should be surfaced like a transport error); (2) cmd_answer prints impact['lines'] and impact['warnings'] but 'unchanged' and 'skipped' produce neither, so silence is ambiguous between 'pass not wired' and 'pass decided nothing'. ACCEPTANCE: (a) `answer --scope bundle` ALWAYS prints one line per walked sibling with the verdict word and score, e.g. 'impact: mcview's D-001 unchanged (score 0.24)'; (b) a verdict with confidence below an explicit T_IMPACT_FLOOR constant is treated as UNKNOWN \u2014 skipped + WARNING, fail-closed; (c) a test asserts the D-003-vs-D-001 scenario prints the score. Evidence repro: namespaces mccli/mcview in DuckBrain, decisions D-003..D-006, shim logs in docs/dogfood/2026-09-23-graph-bundles-integration.md.", "source": "dogfood 2026-09-23 (graph/bundles/