+ {"id": "AUG-029", "title": "[P2] no verb can create bundle/bundle_member rows, membership verification requires the FLEET scheduler DB, and the member-namespace convention (= member's own name) exists only in a code docstring \u2014 SPEC-002 is not usable from the CLI on scratch projects", "status": "pending", "priority": "P2", "type": null, "created_at": "2026-09-23T04:45:00+00:00", "created_by": null, "description": null, "acceptance_criteria": "Dogfood 2026-09-23: bundle B-01 and members BM-0001/2 had to be hand-POSTed to /api/ns/mccli/tables/{bundle,bundle_member}; auger.py has bundle_member() (with three refusals incl. 'project must exist in the scheduler projects table') but NOTHING dispatches to it \u2014 no add_parser entry, no flag on any verb. Consequence: the repo's own dogfood, or any scratch/standalone use, cannot use its own bundle model without raw API calls; and bundle_member()'s scheduler-DB refusal (known_projects() -> SystemExit) makes scratch membership impossible even if a verb existed. Second gap: bundle_namespaces() resolves a member's rows at a namespace NAMED EXACTLY the member (member_namespace = identity, auger.py L865) \u2014 stated nowhere in docs/ (grep member_namespace docs/ = 0 hits); a user pairing namespaces any other way gets silent no-ops (my first attempt put both projects in one namespace and the walk saw nothing). ACCEPTANCE: (a) `auger bundle add <name> [--contract p]` + `auger bundle member <bundle> <project> <role>` verbs, with a documented scratch escape (e.g. AUGER_ALLOW_SCRATCH_MEMBERS=1 skips the scheduler check, printed as a warning); (b) SPEC-002 section 1 and VERBS.md state the namespace convention: 'a member's rows live in the namespace named after the member'; (c) the dogfood integration doc's bundle recipe stops needing curl.", "source": "dogfood 2026-09-23 (graph/bundles/verdict surface)", "review_notes": null, "capability_tags": ["dogfood", "bundles", "cli", "docs", "bundles"], "complexity": 3, "attempts": 0, "